From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:21:10 -0400
Subject: feat: Peek on a held press, and the sidebar's text at 14
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner, 2026-10-25: Peek must be easy to turn off and to tune, on the
setup screen as well as in Settings, and the sidebar's text should be 14.

Peek P18: Settings › Stedding's "Open a peek with" offers a click (as
before), a press held for 0.3 s or one held for 0.5 s. With a hold set, a
plain click on a link in a pinned tab follows it in the tab, and keeping
the mouse button down on the link that long opens the peek. Each tab keeps
the left button's last down and up at its page's widget (PeekPress); the
throttle and the new-tab hook read it with the setting.

Welcome W17: the behaviour step asks how links from pinned tabs open: a
peek on a click, on a 0.3 s or 0.5 s hold, or in the tab (Peek off).
Welcome W18: the appearance step offers the sidebar's text size.

Sidebar Y2: unset, the sidebar's text is 14 (it was the label font's 13 on
the Mac), and a row's room around its text is 16, so 14 keeps every
density's own row height; Settings lists 14 as the default.

Why: the owner's notes on the Peek build.
Removable when: never.
